Problem statement
Sam is researching on Alpha-Triangles. So, he needs to create them for different integers ‘N’.
An Alpha-Triangle is represented by the triangular pattern of alphabets in reverse order.
For every value of ‘N’, help sam to print the corresponding Alpha-Triangle.
Example:

Input: ‘N’ = 3

Output: 
C
C B 
C B A


Solution:

public class Solution {
    public static void alphaTriangle(int n) {
        
        for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {

            
            char c = (char) ('A' + n - 1);
            
            for (int j = 1; j <= i; j++) {

                System.out.print(c + " ");
                c--;
            }
            System.out.println();
        }
    }
}

In Java, characters are backed by numbers (ASCII values). When you do 'A' + n - 1, 
Java calculates the correct character position. Because this calculation results in an integer, 
we add (char) at the front to turn it back into a letter.
